//	control token usage and cost. Truncation will reduce the number of cached
//	tokens on the next turn (busting the cache), since messages are dropped from
//	the beginning of the context. However, clients can also configure truncation
//	to retain messages up to a fraction of the maximum context size, which will
//	reduce the need for future truncations and thus improve the cache rate.
//	Truncation can be disabled entirely, which means the server will never
//	truncate but would instead return an error if the conversation exceeds the
//	model's input token limit.
//	prompt: Reference to a prompt template and its variables. [Learn
//	more](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/text?api-mode=responses#
//	version-prompts-in-code).
