// CreateClientSecret create a Realtime client secret with an associated session configuration. Client secrets are short-lived tokens that can be passed to a client app, such as a web frontend or mobile client, which grants access to the Realtime API without leaking your main API key. You can configure a custom TTL for each client secret. You can also attach session configuration options to the client secret, which will be applied to any sessions created using that client secret, but these can also be overridden by the client connection. [Learn more about authentication with client secrets over WebRTC](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/realtime-webrtc). Returns the created client secret and the effective session object. The client secret is a string that looks like `ek_1234`.
//
// Parameters:
//
//	expiresAfter: Configuration for the client secret expiration. Expiration
//	refers to the time after which a client secret will no longer be valid for
//	creating sessions. The session itself may continue after that time once
//	started. A secret can be used to create multiple sessions until it expires.
//	session: Session configuration to use for the client secret. Choose either a
//	realtime session or a transcription session.
func (sdk *RealtimeNamespace) CreateClientSecret(ctx context.Context, params CreateRealtimeClientSecretParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*RealtimeCreateClientSecretResponse, error) {
	return CreateRealtimeClientSecret(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}
